<title>UK: SBC unit ups two-year bond to 1.5 bln Czech crowns.</title>
<headline>SBC unit ups two-year bond to 1.5 bln Czech crowns.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following, announced earlier by joint lead managers SBC Warburg and Creditanstalt Bankverein, has been increased to 1.5 billion Czech crowns from 1.0 billion Czech crowns.</p>
<p> BORROWER   SWISS BANK CORP (JERSEY BRANCH)</p>
<p> AMT    1.5 BLN CZK   COUPON     10.625    MATURITY    28.JAN.99</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.95    PAY DATE    28.JAN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.25	REOFFER    99.90     SPREAD	 =</p>
<p> MOODY	AA1	 LISTING    LONDON    PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AA+	 DENOMS (K) 25-100    SALE LIMITS US/UK/CZ</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    20 BP     SELL CONC  1.05 PCT  PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	SENIOR, UNSECURED AND UNSUBORDINATED.</p>
<p>		ISSUED OFF A DEBT ISSUANCE PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
